# R21: Narrator lines for the Festival of Fools (places fd_festival, fd_silent_church, fd_ring_of_fools) and the fights' round and phase lines. First draft by Claude, unvoiced.

~ enter:fd_festival
| The village is three times its size and wearing every ribbon it owns. Nobody here is sleeping, and nobody looks tired, and that is the first wrong thing.
| Hand pies steam in doorways that are not doors, and the music has no beginning you can find.
once
~ enter:fd_square
| The Round has squared its shoulders into a fairground, and a clown's face the size of a cart nods over the maypole as if it had been waiting for you to sit down.
once
~ enter:fd_silent_church
| The carnival stops at the door as if cut with a knife. In the sudden quiet you can hear your own boots, and a stone knight listening to them.
once
~ enter:fd_ring_of_fools
| The crowd has drawn back into a ring and holds its breath, still smiling. Six white ribbons run out from the maypole across the packed earth like the spokes of something that is about to turn.
once
~ examine:fd_maypole
| The pole is wound with ribbon in green, red and gold. At the top the balloon's painted mouth is not quite shut.
~ examine:fd_balloon
| A clown the size of a hay wagon, taut and shining, with a grin that was painted by someone who had been told about joy.
~ examine:fd_bonfire_w
| The fire is real enough, and it is the only thing in the square that is not smiling.
~ examine:fd_bonfire_e
| A bonfire, fed by a steady line of dancers who throw in streamers and do not look at what else they throw.
~ examine:fd_ring_pole
| The maypole, wound in ribbons, straining a little against the earth.
~ examine:fd_altar
| The altar is bare timber, still sweet with resin. Someone meant to carve it and did not get to it.
~ fd_brawl_join
| Another costume steps out of the crowd, smiling, and takes the place of the last one.
~ fd_join_dance
| A Herald in motley dances out of the ring to take up the tune.
~ fd_ribbon_bind
| Ribbons snap round your ankles with a sound like a laugh.
~ fd_snack_pelting
| Hand pies and sticky buns rain out of the crowd, thrown with great affection.
~ fd_phase_two
| The balloon swells, the maypole tears loose of the earth, and the painted mouth begins to speak in a voice that has been waiting a long time to be heard.
